[% major_ver = "1.31.9"; version = major_ver _ ".1" -%]
<!---
    @title         OpenResty [% version %] Released
    @description   OpenResty® [% version %] includes Nginx [% major_ver %] with 10 security fixes, updated LuaJIT, and improvements to Lua TLS, locking, and encrypted sessions.
--->

OpenResty [% version %], the new release of the web platform based on NGINX and LuaJIT, is now available.

Get the source distribution and find pre-built Linux packages on the [download page](download.html).

# Version highlights

* **Nginx [% major_ver %] incorporates 10 upstream security fixes** for HTTP/2, HTTP/3, DNS resolution, the mail proxy, HTTP routing and request body handling, and stream TLS. The core also rejects header lines without a colon and chunked request bodies with excessive framing overhead. [Nginx security advisories](https://nginx.org/en/security_advisories.html)
* **Lua TLS APIs** now let applications select TLS ciphers and TLS 1.3 cipher suites during ClientHello processing in HTTP and stream. The updated `lua-resty-openssl` integrates with `lua-resty-core` SSL accessors and the new bundled auxiliary module.
* **Lua shared dictionaries and locks** now support atomic ownership checks. An expired lock owner can no longer release or extend a lock acquired by another caller. Cosocket connection queues and balancer keepalive pools also received updates.
* **LuaJIT** has been updated to v2.1-20261117 and includes fixes for FFI, JIT compilation, and DynASM.

# Upgrade note

`encrypted-session-nginx-module` v0.11 uses a fresh random IV and HMAC-SHA256 for new tokens. Existing tokens are rejected and users need new sessions. Upgrade all instances that exchange tokens before issuing new sessions. [Token format compatibility](https://github.com/openresty/encrypted-session-nginx-module/blob/v0.11/README.md#token-format-compatibility)

